# Rule 2, well-formedness of resolution: an instance with a context whose head
# has no proper part, a bare type parameter or a concrete type, may mention in
# its context only shapes declared before the trait's primary.  Otherwise
# resolving the trait entails the shape, whose requirement calls the trait,
# whose resolution entails the shape: a satisfaction that depends on itself,
# which the compiler reads as unsatisfied and says nothing about.  A context on
# a structured head descends by the head's parts and is not judged here (the
# Paterson conditions).  Declaration order through constraints has no
# clang-query matcher, hence the tool.
tool context-order
